# D-50 (steps/defects.md; FABLE-OPUS-ROOT-TYPED-20260925-175): a negative int compared at the walked
# root.  -1 < 0 holds, so r is 1: Entry 1.  Since -167 commit 2 the walker's LT compares its operands
# as unsigned after loading them at the working width, so an int -1 is a huge value and this row
# exits 0.  NO HARNESS ROW YET: Grok registers it (eternal-runs, Entry 1) with the walker's fix.
int: x 0
x: 0 - 1
int: r 0
if: x < 0
    r: 1
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
